virglrenderer: results written to integer outputs keep their bits

What: the guest's TGSI writes results straight to an integer render target
(it folds floatBitsToUint(f(x)) or uint(i) into "OP OUT[n], ..."). For such a
destination the translation now stores integer results as they are and float
results as their bits (floatBitsToUint/floatBitsToInt):
- integer ops (UADD, AND, NOT, USEQ, FSLT, F2U, TXQ, ...) went through
  uintBitsToFloat()/intBitsToFloat() and were then converted to the output's
  type, i.e. the value of a reinterpreted float;
- SQRT, LRP, DP2/3/4, DPH, DST, LIT, EXP, LOG, SCS, RCP, RSQ, MAD, POW, XPD,
  CMP, UCMP, I2F and U2F wrote without the bit cast: uint(1.0 / x) instead of
  floatBitsToUint(1.0 / x), or a vec4 assigned to a uvec4, which no compiler
  accepts;
- SEQ/SNE/SLT/SGE... applied the bit cast to a bvec4 (does not compile); they
  go through vec4() first.
Float destinations and temporaries get the same GLSL as before.
Why: dEQP-GLES3 builtin_functions.precision.sqrt/length read 315 for
sqrt(99463) instead of its bits; the shaders that did not compile stopped the
guest's whole context. Same on Linux hosts.
Upstream bug (same code upstream); upstreamable; not sent.
Applies after virgl-shader-core-glsl-version.patch.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c "... into an integer color output"
(18 ops; 11 fail without this patch, the others without its first part).
